    "gross_margin": "FY2027Q3 set at the 74.0% guidance midpoint (Q-3; range 73.5%-74.5%). Recent reported margins were about 75.0% in FY2026Q4 (D-2e438021b6 / D-e6100d63c6), 74.9% in FY2027Q1 (F-417baf8cdf / F-e3b41ab7aa) and 75.0% in FY2027Q2 (F-5a54513386 / F-5b8aab8df3), described as roughly flat with Blackwell as the vast majority of revenue (Q-7). The guided step-down to 74.0% coincides with the Vera Rubin introduction (Q-12). Judgment: held at 74.0% for FY2027Q4-FY2028Q2. We assume no further transition dilution and no recovery to 75%. The FY2026Q1 margin of 60.5% (F-c1ec7862bb / F-9221c84b01) was a one-off low and is not used as a base.",
    "opex_pct_revenue": "FY2027Q3: GAAP opex guidance of about $9.2B (Q-4) divided by $108.0B guided revenue (Q-1) = 8.52%. FY2027Q2 GAAP opex was $8,408M (R&D F-e4589deab2 + SG&A F-2725b021df), or 8.74% of revenue, so the guide implies +9.4% q/q opex growth. Opex grew +12.2% in FY2027Q1 (F-e87c3f5cfd + F-44396bc561 vs D-7673c35548 + D-ba914608b4) and +10.3% in FY2027Q2. Later quarters (judgment): opex grows about +9%, +8% and +8% q/q, consistent with that trend, against the revenue path above. That gives 8.44%, 8.44% and 8.52% of revenue. The ratio stays below recent levels because revenue grows faster than opex.",
    "tax_rate": "17.0% = midpoint of the FY2027 GAAP tax rate guidance of 16.0%-18.0%, excluding discrete items (Q-5), applied to all four quarters. The model applies tax to operating income and assumes zero other income/expense (no assumption made for interest or investment gains).",
    "share_change_qoq": "-0.27% per quarter: compound average change in weighted diluted shares from 24,611M (FY2026Q1, F-132c01694e) to 24,285M (FY2027Q2, F-ce6be3a0b0) over five quarters. Buybacks continue: about $26.0B returned in FY2027Q2 through repurchases and dividends (Q-11). The latest quarter's -0.43% (vs F-7b160f6df2) is above the average; we do not extrapolate it."
  }
